@meta
id: 28-11
title: Two mappings worth the space
chapter: 28
type: lesson
skills: vimrc-mappings
par: 215
minutes: 7
vscode: keybindings.json, which nobody on your team has ever opened
open: .vimrc payment.service.ts

@brief
A mapping earns its line in your config by removing something you do
dozens of times a day. Two that almost everyone keeps:

    " leave insert mode without reaching for Esc
    inoremap jk <Esc>
    " clear the search highlight
    nnoremap <leader>h :nohlsearch<CR>

Add both under the existing mappings, source the file, and use the first
one. In the service buffer, the `refund` call needs a timeout option:

    { orderId, timeoutMs: 5000 }

Add `timeoutMs: 5000` after `orderId`, and leave insert mode with `jk`
rather than Esc. If the mapping is not sourced, the letters land in the
file and the check fails.

Use `inoremap`, not `imap`. The `nore` versions map to the keys
themselves rather than to whatever those keys might be mapped to later —
without it, one day you map something involving `<Esc>` and the two
mappings chase each other in a loop. There is no good reason to use the
recursive form until you know exactly why you want it.

@keys
| `inoremap jk <Esc>` | jk leaves insert mode |
| `nnoremap` | normal mode, non-recursive |
| `:source %` | load the file you are editing |
| `:nmap <leader>h` | show what a key is currently mapped to |

@hints
Mapping lines first, then `:w`, then `:source %`, then `:bn`.
--
Comments go on their own line above a mapping, never beside it. Type the
mapping, Esc, then `O` for the comment.
--
`/orderId }` finds the `orderId` inside the object rather than the one
in the signature. `e` goes to the end of the word and `a` appends after
it. End the insert with `jk`, then `:wqa`.

@solution
    G o inoremap jk <Esc> <Esc> O " leave insert mode without reaching for Esc <Esc>
    G o nnoremap <leader>h :nohlsearch<CR> <Esc> O " clear the search highlight <Esc>
    :w<Enter> :source %<Enter> :bn<Enter>
    /orderId }<Enter> e a , timeoutMs: 5000 jk :wqa<Enter>

Note the two `<Esc>` in a row on the first line: one is the five
characters you type into the mapping, the other is the key that ends the
insert. The mapping is not live while you are writing it.

`jk` works because the two letters never occur in that order in text you
type — in English, or in camelCase. `jj` is the other common choice and
has the same property. Both cost you a fraction of a second of delay
after typing a `j`, while vim waits to see whether a `k` is coming; that
is `timeoutlen`, and if it bothers you, that is the next line of config
you add.

`<leader>h` is there for a different reason. `hlsearch` is worth having
and leaves the whole screen yellow after every search, so you need a way
to clear it that does not involve searching for nonsense. `:nohlsearch`
clears the highlight without forgetting the pattern, so `n` still works.

Two habits to keep from here: `nore` unless you can say why not, and one
comment line per mapping. In a year you will not remember what
`<leader>t` did, and the comment is the only thing standing between you
and deleting a line you use every day.

@start .vimrc
" ~/.vimrc - one line at a time, when something annoys you.

set nocompatible
syntax on
filetype plugin indent on

" --- Mappings ---
" space: big, central, and means nothing on its own
let mapleader = " "
nnoremap Y y$
nnoremap <leader>w :w<CR>

@expected .vimrc
" ~/.vimrc - one line at a time, when something annoys you.

set nocompatible
syntax on
filetype plugin indent on

" --- Mappings ---
" space: big, central, and means nothing on its own
let mapleader = " "
nnoremap Y y$
nnoremap <leader>w :w<CR>
" leave insert mode without reaching for Esc
inoremap jk <Esc>
" clear the search highlight
nnoremap <leader>h :nohlsearch<CR>

@start payment.service.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';

@injectable()
export class PaymentService {
  public async refund(orderId: string) {
    return this.gateway.post('/refunds', { orderId });
  }
}

@expected payment.service.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';

@injectable()
export class PaymentService {
  public async refund(orderId: string) {
    return this.gateway.post('/refunds', { orderId, timeoutMs: 5000 });
  }
}
